      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T10:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hey you are right. There\u0027s been few discussions but it\u0027s a bit of a moving target, with new macros added upstream and common practices changing. I changed this to use `DT_COMPAT_GET_ANY_STATUS_OKAY` and added a build check for the instance count, sending a followup for another one I changed recently.\n\nFor best practices, I\u0027d say we should aim at using `DT_COMPAT_GET_ANY_STATUS_OKAY` or `DEVICE_DT_GET_ONE` where we support only one instance, that\u0027s the most compact form, does not require passing nodealiases or phandles around. For devices with multiple instance where we need to refer to a specific one and don\u0027t have a container node, it\u0027s still an open discussion unfortunately.",
